  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Start Alert 723 Colombia Flooding Arauca</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project contributes to mitigating and addressing the effects and protection needs of migrant women and host communities and their families, located in informal human settlements in the municipality of Arauca (Bello Horizonte, Villa Linda, Jabillos, Villa Esperanza, 20 abril), Arauquita (El Oriente), rural districts of Arauca (Monserrate) and Saravena (Isla del Charo (rural area), human settlement 24 de Enero).  Generated by the winter wave that has destroyed roads, losses of crops, equipment, homes, and animals. In addition to accompanying affected families and communities with guidance on key hygiene practices and care tips in the midst of the emergency, through messages to link disaster risk prevention actions. The modality of intervention is chosen when immediate attention in kind is necessary to meet the needs expressed by the communities on elements for hygiene including menstrual care and protection of rain adapted to the cultural traditions and age of the population served.</narrative>
  </description>
